(2 THE TEST LAWS OF PADDLE PONG) Tj T*
(2.1 THE TABLE) Tj T*
(2.1.1 The upper surface of the table, known as the playing surface, shall be rectangular, 3.00 m long and) Tj T*
(1.50 m wide, and shall lie in a horizontal plane 80 cm above the floor.) Tj T*
(2.1.2 The playing surface shall not include the vertical sides of the tabletop; a ball that touches only a) Tj T*
(vertical side has left the playing surface.) Tj T*
(2.1.3 The playing surface shall yield a uniform bounce of about 25 cm when a standard paddle pong ball is) Tj T*
(dropped on to it from a height of 30 cm.) Tj T*
(2.2 THE NET ASSEMBLY) Tj T*
(2.2.1 The net assembly shall consist of the net, its suspension and the supporting posts, including the) Tj T*
(clamps attaching them to the table.) Tj T*
(2.2.2 The top of the net, along its whole length, shall be 16 cm above the playing surface.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2.6 THE SERVICE) Tj T*
(2.6.1 Service shall start with the ball resting freely on the open palm of the server's stationary free) Tj T*
(hand, held still for at least one second.) Tj T*
(2.6.2 The server shall then project the ball near vertically upwards, without imparting spin, so that it) Tj T*
(rises at least 20 cm after leaving the palm of the free hand and then falls without touching anything) Tj T*
(before being struck.) Tj T*
(2.6.3 As the ball is falling the server shall strike it so that it touches first the server's own court and) Tj T*
(then, after passing over or around the net assembly, touches directly the receiver's court.) Tj T*
(2.6.4 From the start of service until it is struck, the ball shall be above the level of the playing surface) Tj T*
(and behind the server's end line, and it shall not be hidden from the receiver.) Tj T*
(2.6.5 As soon as the ball has been projected, the server's free arm and hand shall be removed from the space) Tj T*
(between the ball and the net.) Tj T*
(National byelaw 2.6.5\(a\): in domestic league play the referee may waive the free-arm requirement for) Tj T*
(players under twelve. This paragraph is a byelaw box and must be skipped by the scraper.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2.9 A LET) Tj T*
(2.9.1 The rally shall be a let if in service the ball, in passing over or around the net assembly, touches) Tj T*
(it, provided the service is otherwise correct or the ball is obstructed by the receiver.) Tj T*
(2.9.2 The rally shall be a let if the service is delivered when the receiving player or pair is not ready,) Tj T*
(provided that neither the receiver nor the receiver's partner attempts to strike the ball.) Tj T*
(2.9.3 The rally shall be a let if play is interrupted by the umpire or assistant umpire for any reason.) Tj T*
(2.10 A POINT) Tj T*
(2.10.1 Unless the rally is a let, a player shall score a point if the opponent fails to make a correct) Tj T*
ET
