() Tj T*
(2.11 A GAME) Tj T*
(2.11.1 A game shall be won by the player or pair first scoring 15 points unless both players or pairs score) Tj T*
(14 points, when the game shall be won by the first player or pair subsequently gaining a lead of 2 points.) Tj T*
(2.13 THE ORDER OF SERVING) Tj T*
(2.13.1 After each 3 points have been scored the receiving player or pair shall become the serving player or) Tj T*
(pair and so on until the end of the game, unless both players or pairs score 14 points, when the sequence) Tj T*
(of serving and receiving shall be the same but each player shall serve for only 1 point in turn.) Tj T*
(2.13.2 The player or pair who served first in a game shall receive first in the next game of the match.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2.14 EQUIPMENT CHECKS) Tj T*
(2.14.1 Before a match the umpire shall inspect every racket. A racket may be of any size, shape or weight) Tj T*
(but the blade shall be flat and rigid. At least 85 percent of the blade by thickness shall be of natural wood;) Tj T*
(an adhesive layer within the blade may be reinforced with fibrous material such as carbon fibre, glass fibre) Tj T*
(or compressed paper, but shall not be thicker than 7.5 percent of the total thickness or 0.35 mm, whichever) Tj T*
(is the smaller. A side of the blade used for striking the ball shall be covered with either ordinary) Tj T*
(pimpled rubber, with pimples outwards having a total thickness including adhesive of not more than 2.0 mm,) Tj T*
(or sandwich rubber, with pimples inwards or outwards, having a total thickness including adhesive of not) Tj T*
(more than 4.0 mm. Ordinary pimpled rubber is a single layer of non-cellular rubber, natural or synthetic,) Tj T*
(with pimples evenly distributed over its surface at a density of not less than 10 per square centimetre and) Tj T*
(not more than 30 per square centimetre. Sandwich rubber is a single layer of cellular rubber covered with a) Tj T*
(single outer layer of ordinary pimpled rubber, the thickness of the pimpled rubber not being more than 2.0) Tj T*
(mm. The covering material shall extend up to but not beyond the limits of the blade, except that the part) Tj T*
(nearest the handle and gripped by the fingers may be left uncovered or covered with any material. The) Tj T*
(blade, any layer within the blade and any layer of covering material or adhesive on a side used for) Tj T*
(striking the ball shall be continuous and of even thickness. The surface of the covering material on a) Tj T*
(side of the blade, or of a side of the blade if it is left uncovered, shall be matt, bright red on one side) Tj T*
(and black on the other. The racket covering shall be used without any physical, chemical or other) Tj T*
(treatment. Slight deviations from continuity of surface or uniformity of colour due to accidental damage) Tj T*
(or wear may be allowed provided that they do not significantly change the characteristics of the surface.) Tj T*
(Before the start of a match and whenever a player changes a racket during a match the player shall show the) Tj T*
(opponent and the umpire the racket that is about to be used and shall allow them to examine it. The umpire) Tj T*
(shall record the colours used and shall report any racket that fails inspection to the referee, who shall) Tj T*
(decide whether it may be used for the remainder of the match or must be replaced before play continues.) Tj T*
(2.14.2 A ball shall be spherical, with a diameter of 42 mm, shall weigh 3.0 g and shall be made of) Tj T*
(celluloid or similar plastics material and shall be white or orange, and matt.) Tj T*
